  "purpose": "Deterministic mapping from source-tree paths to the CAP-XXX capabilities they belong to. Consumed by the HQ Security Agent (ADR-0316a) at every proposed code change. If a proposed change touches a file whose path does not match any pattern here, the Security Agent rejects with `sec.file_outside_registry`. This registry is the file-level manifestation of NEX's capability map · Work Map (docs/nex-work-map.json) is the capability-level manifestation.",
  "constitutional_rule": "Every file in src/**/* · db/**/* · scripts/**/* · docs/**/* MUST map to exactly one owning CAP-XXX via the patterns below. Missing map = HQ Security Agent REJECT (sec.file_outside_registry). Overlapping patterns resolved by precedence (higher precedence wins).",
  "constitutional_rule_v2": "Adding a new file requires either (a) an existing pattern already covering it · or (b) an ADR-authorised amendment to this registry adding a new pattern. Silent introduction of files under unregistered paths is a Guardian violation.",
  "fallback_action": "reject",
  "fallback_rejection_code": "sec.file_outside_registry",
  "precedence_rule": "Later entries override earlier entries when patterns overlap. Author more specific patterns AFTER more general ones.",
  "capability_reference": "docs/nex-work-map.json",
